  "adaptationPolicy": {
    "cratePaths": "crate:: becomes crate::svg_engine::<source engine>::, including rustdoc links",
    "resvgUsvgPaths": "resvg/lib.rs retains its used internal alias; all other resvg usvg:: paths become crate::svg_engine::usvg::",
    "harfrustAlias": "usvg harfrust:: becomes svg_harfrust:: (original 0.12 dependency identity)",
    "enabledFeaturePredicates": "The original enabled feature counts are retained per file; constant evaluation removes 79 true cfg attributes and four false branches. OS and test conditions are retained; KRR has no optional public SVG-engine feature contract.",
    "allowAttributes": "The original 46 allow attributes are retained verbatim. Two scoped boundary attributes permit observed external Clippy lints (22 in usvg/lib.rs, 18 in resvg/lib.rs) plus dead_code and unused_imports. Four resvg lints already allowed upstream are omitted from the added list to avoid duplicate attributes. No blanket all, non_minimal_cfg, unsafe-code override, or additional exclusion is introduced.",
    "sourceSemantics": "Initial mechanical transplant preserves upstream behavior; subsequent scoped fixes pass CSS font size to HarfRust tracking and use hard-edge clipping only for implicit marker viewports. An optional internal fallback callback receives the original requested font attributes while the default legacy resolver remains unchanged; nested SVG forwards the callback. Original SVG, glyph IDs, and variation coordinates are not manually rewritten. Clip bounds, user-clip antialiasing, and upstream test expectations are preserved. ViewBox scale and alignment use f64 intermediate arithmetic before conversion to the existing f32 transform. Linked feImage parsing transfers a child ID only to an unnamed parent and preserves existing referenced IDs across serialization. Skrifa 0.49 compatibility uses the optional SVG glyph-data accessor and reads opsz axis presence from the same face metadata. Upstream source hashes and licenses remain unchanged."
  },
